w questions from the  audience and then we'll wrap up why  don't Kanellis why don't you come down  here and tell us that and then we'll  then we'll close on that  first you first thank you for the  opportunity give me the talk sorry for  my bad english about the the last moment  you know there when I was pedaling in  towards to Santorini was the tailwind so  no problem no big problems and over  there as John said because of the high  speed we had they decide to make me do a  turn so we did the turn but during the  turn we face the wind and the wind  approaching the land was too hard so the  plane was going up and down like you  have seen there this plane was not  designed to do all those things so it  resisted too much and one moment I felt  no it was not my feeling was real the  plane was flying but staying in the same  place because they wind had the speed of  the plane so it was very tough and then  he took a bank you know and it was not  possible to make it return back so he  did once he did twice and then broken  the the tail so it was but it was closed  but I think this this end because was  not so easy and smooth like the other  make a very you know put fear to someone  else who wants to do the same that is  not so easy  well with that I think we'll will  conclude this year's Gardner lecture  thank you very much for coming  [Applause]

